# deploy/pi/cloudflared-config.yml.example
#
# Copy to the Pi and replace the placeholders:
#   sudo install -o root -g root -m 0600 deploy/pi/cloudflared-config.yml.example /etc/cloudflared/config.yml
#
# The tunnel credentials JSON produced by `cloudflared tunnel login` /
# `cloudflared tunnel create` must also stay root-only at
# /etc/cloudflared/<TUNNEL_ID>.json. Neither file is ever committed.
#
# PUBLIC SURFACE RULE: this ingress table is the entire public attack surface
# of the Pi. Exactly one hostname (the relay) plus a catch-all 404. There is
# deliberately NO rule for SSH, the Fleetdeck panel, /readyz, metrics, or the
# SQLite database.

tunnel: <REPLACE_WITH_TUNNEL_ID>
credentials-file: /etc/cloudflared/<REPLACE_WITH_TUNNEL_ID>.json

ingress:
  # Public entry point: the bug-report relay and nothing else.
  - hostname: bugs.<REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DOMAIN>
    service: http://127.0.0.1:8787
    # Cloudflare-side protection (set in the Cloudflare dashboard, not here):
    #   - WAF managed rules for this hostname
    #   - Rate limiting on POST /v1/reports (relay already limits per-IP + daily budget)
    #   - Bot fight mode, and "Under Attack" while responding to an incident
  # Catch-all: any other hostname routed to this tunnel returns HTTP 404.
  - service: http_status:404
